My project is a prompt injection testing framework for a locally running large language model. I used Python, Ollama,
and Qwen3:8B to test whether a fictional banking assistant could be manipulated into disclosing a dummy secret placed in its system prompt.

I conducted two experiments. The single-turn benchmark tested 120 independent prompts and recorded 26 exact-secret leaks,
giving an attempt-level leak rate of 21.67%. The multi-turn experiment tested 10 scenarios over 20 successful responses and 
recorded one exact-secret leak, or 5% at the turn level.

The most interesting case occurred in the second turn of a role-play scenario. The project demonstrates a disclosure failure under the tested configuration, but its results are exploratory and do not establish the security of all LLMs.
